# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-16, R-6, RC-5; L §5.19 Readings at a place that keeps parts). L §5.19 Stated parts: "rows of the reading input with of: stated[x] of q = v at the reading's instant and, where the
# walk starts, opening[x] of q = v ... They stand beside the reading's total, in the same version and at the same instant
# (LOAD-PARTS otherwise), and sum to at most it (LOAD-PARTS where load sees both, RUN-RECORD otherwise); the rest of the
# total, if any, is the unstated rest".
# The opening states 150.00, ania's 100.00: the unstated rest, 50.00 (scratch/exp7.py), is a hole part that can't be
# ania's, so tomek's is HOLE-PART and ania's is known.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-31), bal(konto, 2026-01-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-01-31) of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 150.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto] of ania = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
q: (150.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN, ?"konto: 50.00 PLN may be tomek's: whose are 50.00 PLN of konto at 2026-01-01 start?" (konto))
  cut 2026-01-01
